On Wed, May 29, 2013 at 8:19 AM, tijlan <jbotijlan@gmail.com> wrote:

>
> From the perspective of branching,
>
> ME + sumti
> NU + sentence
> NOI + sentence
> ...
>
> are analogous to
>
> tag + sumti
>
> or rather to
>
> selbri + sumti.
>
> ME/NU/NOI/... share the same relative position as selbri, as heads,
> followed by modifiers: modification expands rightward.
>

It could be argued that in

ME sumti MEhU
NU sentence KEI
NOI sentence KUhO

the complement is infixed into the head, rather than to its right.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

